{"name":"Fish Tale","hex":"#015e6a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fish tale","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of fish story (“tall tale”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish_tale"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fish Tales (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Fish Tales is a 12\"-EP by New Zealand band the 3Ds, released in 1990."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/16/Fish_Tales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish_Tales_(EP)"},{"title":"Fish Tales (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fish Tales is a 1936 American animated comedy short film directed by Jack King. The short was released on May 23, 1936. It is the 71st film in the Looney Tunes series and the eighth cartoon to feature Porky Pig."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Fish_Tales.png/330px-Fish_Tales.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish_Tales_(film)"},{"title":"Fish","blocks":[{"text":"A fish is an aquatic, anamniotic, gill-bearing vertebrate animal with a tough cranium to protect the brain, but lacking limbs with digits. Fish can be grouped into the more basal jawless fish and the more common jawed fish, the latter including all living cartilaginous and bony fish, as well as the extinct placoderms and acanthodians. Tetrapods are descended from fish, so in a break from the long tradition of grouping all fish into a single class (Pisces), modern phylogenetics views fish as a paraphyletic group that includes all vertebrates except tetrapods. To treat fish as a monophyletic group, one would have to classify tetrapods as a clade/subgroup of specialized fish, which would make \"fish\" and \"vertebrates\" synonyms. In English, the plural of \"fish\" is fish when referring to individuals and fishes when referring to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Dunkleosteus_profile.jpg/500px-Dunkleosteus_profile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Dunkleosteus_profile.jpg/1280px-Dunkleosteus_profile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Dunkleosteus_profile.jpg/500px-Dunkleosteus_profile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dunkleosteus was a giant Devonian armoured placoderm, c. 400 mya.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADunkleosteus_profile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/A_Galeaspid.jpg/330px-A_Galeaspid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/A_Galeaspid.jpg/330px-A_Galeaspid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Galeaspid.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Diplacanthus_reconstructed.jpg/500px-Diplacanthus_reconstructed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Diplacanthus_reconstructed.jpg/1280px-Diplacanthus_reconstructed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Diplacanthus_reconstructed.jpg/500px-Diplacanthus_reconstructed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip